---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service — Hotel Menu Guide"
  description="Terms of service for Hotel Menu Guide: informational content, price accuracy, and acceptable use."
  path="/terms-of-service/"
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-soft">Last updated: September 30, 2026</p>

    <div class="prose-guide mt-6">
      <h2>What this site provides</h2>
      <p>
        Hotel Menu Guide publishes informational guides about restaurant menus. The content is
        provided as-is for general information only. It is not a reservation service, and we are
        not affiliated with any hotel or restaurant mentioned.
      </p>
      <h2>Prices and accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        Menus and prices change frequently. We date our reported prices (currently as of September
        2026) and show ranges where sources disagree, but we can't guarantee any figure is current.
        Always verify prices, hours, and availability with the restaurant before visiting. We
        accept no liability for decisions made based on this site's content.
      </p>
      <h2>Original content</h2>
      <p>
        All text and illustrations on this site are original. Restaurant and hotel names are used
        nominatively to identify the subjects of our guides; all trademarks belong to their
        respective owners.
      </p>
      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        You're welcome to read, link to, and share our pages. Don't scrape the site's content at
        scale, misrepresent it as your own, or use it in a way that harms the site or its readers.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms as the site evolves. Continued use of the site after changes
        means you accept the updated terms.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
